# Keeps the build context (and both Dockerfiles' COPYs) free of host-side
# build artifacts and dependency trees. Without this, `COPY backends
# ./backends` / `COPY frontends ./frontends` would also ship this machine's
# own `target/` (Rust, host-arch, gigabytes) and every `node_modules/`
# (potentially host-arch native binaries) straight into the build context —
# wasting cache and, for node_modules, risking a macOS/arm64 native module
# being copied into a linux/alpine build.

# Rust
/target
**/target

# Node / pnpm
**/node_modules
.next/
**/.next/
storybook-static/
dist/
**/dist/
.turbo/
**/.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# VCS / editor / OS
.git
.github
.DS_Store
*.log

# Local env files (never belong in an image layer)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test artifacts
cypress/screenshots/
cypress/videos/

# Docs — not needed inside either build context
docs/
